.\" garnet(1) — the Garnet command-line toolchain.
.\" The .deb and .rpm packages install this page at /usr/share/man/man1/garnet.1;
.\" the macOS .pkg script installs it under /usr/local/share/man/man1/.
.\" The SUBCOMMANDS section must list exactly the subcommands `garnet --help`
.\" prints, and the .TH line names no release (`garnet --version` reports it);
.\" garnet-cli/tests/man_page.rs fails when either drifts.
.TH GARNET 1 "2026-09-11" "garnet" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
garnet \- the Garnet dual-mode language toolchain

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B garnet
.I SUBCOMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.br
.B garnet \-\-version
.br
.B garnet \-\-help

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B garnet
is the command-line driver for Garnet, a research-grade language prototype
(v0.x, not a 1.0 production release).
Garnet has two modes in one grammar: managed mode (\fIdef\fR, ARC and
exceptions) feels like Ruby; safe mode (\fI@safe\fR, \fIfn\fR, ownership and
\fIResult\fR) feels like Rust.
The mode boundary bridges errors and ownership automatically.
.PP
Functions declare the OS authority they need with \fI@caps(...)\fR, and the
checker verifies those declarations transitively across named, acyclic calls.
The trust-spine subcommands (\fBcaps\fR, \fBdiff\-caps\fR, \fBseal\fR,
\fBcaps\-log\fR, \fBagent\-loop\fR and the \fBverify\fR acceptance gate) turn
that capability surface into manifests, diffs, attestations, a transparency
log and acceptance decisions.

.SH SUBCOMMANDS

.SS Projects

.TP
.B new \-\-template \fITEMPLATE\fR \fIDIR\fR
Scaffold a new project at \fIDIR\fR.
\fITEMPLATE\fR is \fBcli\fR, \fBweb\-api\fR or \fBagent\-orchestrator\fR
(Researcher, Synthesizer and Reviewer actors).

.TP
.B add \fIPATH\fR \fR[\fB\-\-name\fR \fIID\fR]
Vendor a local Garnet directory into \fI.garnet/vendor\fR.
This is not a package registry.

.TP
.B test \fR[\fIDIR\fR]
Discover and run every function whose name starts with \fBtest_\fR in the
project's \fItests/*.garnet\fR files.

.SS Language

.TP
.B parse \fR[\fB\-\-mode\fR \fBast\fR|\fBcst\fR] \fIFILE\fR
Parse \fIFILE\fR and print a structural summary.

.TP
.B check \fR[\fB\-\-suggest\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR \fBhuman\fR|\fBjson\fR] \fIFILE\fR
Run the safe-mode checker.
Its CapCaps propagator reports an annotated function whose declared
\fI@caps(...)\fR does not cover what its named, acyclic calls reach; see
CAPABILITY MODEL for the limits.
\fB\-\-format json\fR emits structured diagnostics.

.TP
.B run \fIFILE\fR
Parse and load \fIFILE\fR, then invoke \fBmain\fR if the module defines one.

.TP
.B eval \fI"EXPR"\fR
Evaluate a single expression and print the result.

.TP
.B repl \fR[\fIFILE\fR]
Start an interactive REPL, optionally preloading \fIFILE\fR.

.TP
.B fmt \fR[\fB\-\-check\fR|\fB\-\-stdout\fR] \fIFILE\fR
Normalize the whitespace of a Garnet source file.

.TP
.B doc \fR[\fB\-\-stdout\fR|\fB\-\-out\fR \fIPATH\fR] \fIFILE\fR
Extract \fB///\fR doc comments into a Markdown summary.

.TP
.B doctest \fR[\fB\-\-format\fR \fBhuman\fR|\fBjson\fR] \fIFILE\fR
Run the Garnet code examples in \fB///\fR doc comments.

.SS Trust spine

.TP
.B caps \fR[\fB\-\-standard\-profile\fR] \fIPATH\fR
Emit the capability manifest for \fIPATH\fR, or with
\fB\-\-standard\-profile\fR the S98 draft standard profile.

.TP
.B diff\-caps \fR[\fB\-\-machine\fR] \fIOLD\fR \fINEW\fR
Diff two capability surfaces.
Exits nonzero when \fINEW\fR grants authority \fIOLD\fR did not.
\fB\-\-machine\fR prints a deterministic single-line JSON verdict for
automated reviewers.

.TP
.B seal \fIFILE\fR
Emit an in-toto attestation (a seal) for \fIFILE\fR, ready for cosign to sign.

.TP
.B caps\-log \fIFILE\fR \fR[\fB\-\-log\fR \fIPATH\fR] | \fB\-\-verify\fR \fILOG\fR
Print a hash-chained entry recording the capability surface of \fIFILE\fR;
with \fB\-\-log\fR, append it to the local file \fIPATH\fR.
\fB\-\-verify\fR checks the hash chain of a local log.
This is a local stub: there is no witness, signed tree head or inclusion
proof.

.TP
.B agent\-loop \-\-baseline \fIOLD\fR \fB\-\-proposal\fR \fINEW\fR
Accept agent-authored code only when diff-caps and enforced-kernel evidence
support it, then seal it.

.TP
.B verify \fIPATH\fR \fR[\fB\-\-external\-band\fR \fI1\-5\fR] [\fB\-\-caps\-baseline\fR \fIOLD\fR]
Acceptance gate: an edition-aware parse and safe-mode check that reports a
merge-confidence band, the minimum of the signals present: the internal
check, plus \fB\-\-external\-band\fR and the diff-caps comparison when given.
A low band alone does not fail the command; a fatal finding does.

.TP
.B trust\-report \fIFILE\fR
Print a structural trust report: actor and thread counts and the capability
surface.

.TP
.B sandbox \fR[\fB\-\-format\fR \fBhuman\fR|\fBjson\fR] \fIFILE\fR
Generate the seccomp, WASI and egress policy implied by the declared
\fI@caps(...)\fR of \fIFILE\fR.
Generation only: this subcommand enforces nothing.

.TP
.B mcp\-caps \fR[\fB\-\-format\fR \fBhuman\fR|\fBjson\fR] \fIFILE\fR
Report the capability surface of an MCP tool set.

.TP
.B mcp\-serve \-\-package \fIDIR\fR
Serve the one verified local Shelf package over raw-byte stdio.

.TP
.B bounds \fIFILE\fR
Report the declared \fI@bounded(N)\fR fuel budgets (the Wasmtime-fuel target).
Fuel budgets are declared, not enforced.

.TP
.B ceilings \fIFILE\fR
Identify explosive operations (loops and spawns) and the default-ceiling
policy.

.TP
.B concurrency \fIFILE\fR
Report the actor concurrency contract (ask and tell protocols).

.SS Build and release

.TP
.B build \fR[\fB\-\-deterministic\fR] [\fB\-\-sign\fR \fIKEYFILE\fR] \fIFILE\fR
Parse \fIFILE\fR and report its item count.
With \fB\-\-deterministic\fR, also write a provenance manifest, which records
the source and AST hashes, to \fIFILE\fB.manifest.json\fR.
\fB\-\-sign\fR requires \fB\-\-deterministic\fR and signs that manifest with
the Ed25519 key stored in \fIKEYFILE\fR.

.TP
.B verify \fIFILE\fR \fIMANIFEST\fR \fR[\fB\-\-signature\fR]
Check that \fIMANIFEST\fR matches a fresh build of \fIFILE\fR.
A signed manifest always needs a valid Ed25519 signature;
\fB\-\-signature\fR also rejects an unsigned one.

.TP
.B keygen \fIKEYFILE\fR
Generate an Ed25519 signing keypair: write the signing key to \fIKEYFILE\fR
and print the public key.

.TP
.B convert \fILANG\fR \fIFILE\fR
Convert Rust, Ruby, Python or Go source to Garnet.
Writes the converted \fI.garnet\fR file with a \fI.lineage.json\fR,
a \fI.migrate_todo.md\fR checklist and a \fI.metrics.json\fR summary.
The output carries \fI@sandbox\fR; lifting it is a human decision.

.SS Information

.TP
.B version
Print the toolchain versions and the wordmark.

.TP
.B help
Print the subcommand summary.

.SH CAPABILITY MODEL
A function declares its OS authority with \fI@caps(...)\fR.
\fBgarnet check\fR follows named calls from each annotated function, through
unannotated helpers, and reports a coverage error when a capability the chain
needs is missing from the declaration: if \fBmain\fR declares \fI@caps()\fR
and calls a helper that calls \fIread_file\fR, it reports that \fBmain\fR does
not declare \fBfs\fR.
The check has limits.
It builds no edge for a call through a function value (an alias, a
parameter, an actor handler), inside a closure or a string interpolation, or
through \fImethod_missing\fR; it does not check the body of an unannotated
function on its own; and a primitive reached only through a cycle of calls is
not reported.
\fBgarnet run\fR does not run the checker.
\fBmain\fR must declare its capabilities; \fI@caps()\fR is correct for a
program that needs none.
.PP
The capabilities are \fBfs\fR (file-system read and write), \fBnet\fR
(public TCP/UDP), \fBnet_internal\fR (RFC 1918 and loopback TCP/UDP),
\fBenv\fR (process environment), \fBproc\fR (process spawn and signals),
\fBtime\fR (wall clock and sleep), \fBffi\fR (\fIextern "C"\fR calls) and
\fB*\fR (a wildcard, rejected in safe-mode functions).
\fBnet_internal\fR and \fBffi\fR are checker vocabulary only: no runtime
primitive is gated on them.

.SH ENFORCEMENT SCOPE
At run time, \fI@caps\fR is enforced for the 15 entry-gated host primitives:
the file-system calls (\fIread_file\fR, \fIwrite_file\fR, \fIread_bytes\fR,
\fIwrite_bytes\fR, \fIlist_dir\fR), \fInet::tcp_connect\fR, the environment
and process calls, and \fIstd::log::to_file\fR.
Calling one traps unless both the calling chain and the program's entry
function declare the capability.
The \fBtime\fR primitives and UUID v4/v7 need \fI@caps(time)\fR at check time
only and run undeclared.
\fI@max_depth\fR is enforced.
Both hold identically in the tree-walking interpreter and the bytecode VM.
.PP
\fI@bounded\fR fuel budgets, memory and time limits, and the \fI@mailbox\fR
annotation are declared but not enforced.
.PP
\fBgarnet sandbox\fR generates a seccomp, WASI and egress policy and applies
none of it.
On Linux that policy has been applied, and shown to trap, by a separate C
reference harness (\fItools/seccomp\-apply\fR in the source repository) that
these packages do not install; on macOS and Windows it is not applied.
.PP
The full table is
\fIC_Language_Specification/GARNET_CAPABILITY_ENFORCEMENT_SCOPE.md\fR in the
source repository.

.SH EXAMPLES
Create a new CLI project and run it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
garnet new \-\-template cli my_app
cd my_app
garnet run src/main.garnet
.fi
.RE
.PP
Build a reproducible, signed manifest and verify it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
garnet keygen my.key
garnet build \-\-deterministic \-\-sign my.key src/main.garnet
garnet verify src/main.garnet src/main.garnet.manifest.json \-\-signature
.fi
.RE
.PP
Convert a Ruby file to Garnet:
.PP
.RS
.nf
garnet convert ruby legacy.rb
.fi
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command ran and reported a problem: for example a checker diagnostic, a
file that cannot be read, or a \fBdiff\-caps\fR result in which the new
surface grants more authority.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error (an unknown subcommand, a missing argument or a malformed
flag), and also a failed manifest check by
\fBverify\fR \fIFILE\fR \fIMANIFEST\fR.
.PP
Scripts should treat any nonzero status as failure.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I .garnet\-cache/episodes.log
Per-project log of CLI invocations.
Each record carries a BLAKE3 keyed MAC under a per-machine key; records that
fail it are skipped.
Machine-specific; do not commit it.
.TP
.I .garnet/vendor/
Local directories vendored by \fBgarnet add\fR.
.TP
.I FILE\fB.manifest.json\fR
The manifest written by \fBgarnet build \-\-deterministic\fR.

